    backlog:hasTestSpec "Deck of chapter 24 (Text-to-Speech and Speech Recognition Engines), 26 slides, notes 26/26 (re-read by the lineage session with python-pptx). Reported by the building agent: structure 0 paragraphs PowerPoint would repair; deck_check 12 console rows, 2 charts and 4 tables recomputed, 0 mismatches; program_check 23 panels from 17 programs, each recorded twice with equal transcripts and re-run, exit 0; 5 pictures byte-identical; diagram_check 7 diagrams, 71 labels verbatim; layout clean; fit 0 overflows and 0 overlaps; notes PASS; honesty_check 0 refusals (15 stand-in slides, 5 NOT EXECUTED, 12 Recorded); links_check 14/14 below 400; the 16 stale fixtures of chapter 23 plus a 17th (stale_standin_remote) refused by the checks that own them; re-encoded control accepted. NOT EXECUTED slides 5, 8, 12, 19, 23 (SAPI5, macOS, AVSpeech; Whisper medium/turbo killed at ~6 GB and large-v3 not loading are shown as findings; YouTube download; cloud services, microphone, other engines). Recorded slides 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 11, 12, 15, 18, 19, 20, 23. Stated deviations: honesty_check gained a standin_remote kind and a plain kind, program_check a run cache, the build a REUSE_RECORDING option; archive.org public-domain audio stands in for YouTube; several single-run numbers differ from the research and are noted on slides or in notes; the deck_build file was assembled by concatenating sections kept in scratch." ;
