ex:ST_Page_Threads backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-14T11:17:27"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-14T11:17:27"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev_Page_Threads ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid .
ex:Ev_Page_Threads a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Checks for Page Threads"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Page/Threads" ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "Page of the Threads subject (file slot 25): NEW template 9.50.0 (examples held in one exec('...') expression offered junk fill-in-the-blank tokens and failed the exercise and exam checks; it now offers only the program's own tokens, reads escaped quotes, applies the while guard to program lines only, and looks among 20 tokens for one that makes the output fail or differ; plain code is read as before; chapters 19 to 22 are affected only if rebuilt), builder 4.17.0, test 9.34.0, register 1.54.0, config 1.20.0 (corpus.book is [] because the 3rd edition has no such chapter; a config for a 3rd-edition chapter must restore the {nn} pattern), page-data 2.23.0. Reported by the building agent: page test twice: 372 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped each run (the same two ERD skips). Gates OVERALL PASS with argument 25; checks script 83 checks 0 mismatches. 4 of 64 examples run in the browser and equal the recording (Join before start, Lock released on error, Lock not reentrant, the lock on in the standard build); 60 are Recorded with reasons (22 cannot start a thread, 12 start a child interpreter, 3 need the local stand-in server, 3 fetch with urllib without https, 11 read the repository's timing record, 3 run asyncio, 6 print something different in the browser). In the browser's Pyodide 0.28.2 (Python 3.13.2) Thread.start, Timer.start and ThreadPoolExecutor.submit/map raise RuntimeError: can't start new thread, while Lock, Event and Queue work in the single thread; this was checked at build time and stated in the page's limits entry. Playground: a lost-updates simulation in plain Python that then tries a real thread and prints what happened. 1 hash-checked picture (skipped-comics grid) drawn against the local stand-in server; the real xkcd.com was never contacted. Deck labels reproduced (NOT EXECUTED slides 11, 18, 20, 23; Recorded 4, 9, 18, 19, 20, 21, 23). No approved outcome is claimed as served. The lineage session did not re-run the page test. OPEN LICENCE QUESTION: the book's online materials (not embedded). Not verified: exam release with the real key; live LLM; Chrome and Safari; Windows and macOS; Python 3.14.7+/3.15; free-threaded behaviour in a browser; earlier pages under template 9.50.0; the Courseware attestation, the owner's, pending and not claimed." ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Checks run by the building agent over the page committed in 6c960b4 (file slot ch25); research package v1_0_0." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "the page test in headless Chromium (playwright 1.56.0); sen0414_rdodi_gates_v1_1_1.py and Stage 4 checks as reported" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-14T11:17:27"^^xsd:dateTime .
