ex:CR2_Standard a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Bring the decks and interactive pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8 to the written teaching-material standard, with the slide code in a chapter-code tab of the page"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope2 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's request of Friday 2026-10-23 08:57 Istanbul (05:57 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator in the assignment to the lineage agent and recorded here as relayed (a statement of its content, not a verbatim quotation, because the lineage agent holds the assignment, not a transcript of the owner's message): the PPT decks and interactive HTML pages of SEN0414 chapters 6 (Lists), 7 (Dictionaries) and 8 must meet the same standards as the sibling course SEN0401 chapters 5 and 6 just delivered, especially that the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in a special 'chapter code' tab of the page that can run it. The request is urgent: the owner's class material is needed as soon as possible, and decks and pages ship chapter by chapter as each is controlled. The request is direction from the owner and authorises the scope; the length of the iteration remains his to decide. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. The change grows the scope: this lineage admitted the finished chapters 7 to 12 exactly as they stand and excluded any rebuild; the owner now asks for new decks and pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8 and for the tools that measure the standard, as new files beside the Done ones. Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the stories is recorded in the Backlog version." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_Standard a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What bringing the chapter 6, 7 and 8 decks and pages to the written standard costs, with the facts measured before it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_Standard ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, read-only, 2026-10-23; tools: python-pptx 1.0.2 and Playwright 1.56.0; the deck figures come from a straight substitution port of the sibling's deck standard check made in the lineage agent's scratch folder, outside the repository, so the independent tool the first task writes must reproduce or explain every number below; a difference is reported, not adjusted). DECKS. Chapter 6 (03-materials/ch06/SEN0414_Ch06_Lists_3e_v2_0_0.pptx): 26 slides, 12 code slides, 3 native charts, 27 research concepts; elements failing: D1 (25 of 26 slides numbered; the first is not), D2 (longest box 102 words, 17 boxes over 30), D3 (3 of 12 code slides carry both the explanation and a visual result), D4 (12 of 27 key concepts have an analogy), D5 (0 of 4 story slides complete), D7 (25 slides with notes over 60 words, longest 240), D10 (0 of 3 dividers complete), D11 (15 of 27 concepts on a slide = 55.6 percent); D6, D8, D9, D12 pass. Chapter 7 (03-materials/ch07/SEN0414_Ch07_Dictionaries_3e_v1_0_0.pptx): 26 slides, 9 code slides, 1 native chart, 34 concepts; D1, D2 (longest 130 words), D3 (0 of 9), D4 (0 of 34), D5 (0 of 4), D7 (longest note 168 words), D11 (17 of 34 = 50.0 percent) fail; D10 not measured (no divider found); D6, D8, D9, D12 pass. Chapter 8 (the only deck, 08-tooling/ch08-deck/sen0414_ch08_deck_v1_0_0.pptx; 03-materials/ch08 holds no deck): 25 slides, 13 code slides, 0 native charts, 57 concepts; D1, D2 (longest 90 words), D3 (0 of 13), D4 (0 of 57), D5 (0 of 4), D7 (longest note 140), D11 (31 of 57 = 54.4 percent) fail; D10 not measured; D6, D8, D9, D12 pass. Discrepancy to be settled by the independent tool and not adjusted: the owner's own measurement of the chapter 8 deck reported a failure of D8 (resources slide); the port reads D8 PASS (a resources slide, slide 24, with 11 external links). PAGES (the shipped pages sen0414_chNN_page_v9_28_0.html, template line 9.50.0, page test 9.34.0). None of the three pages has a chapter-code tab (0 elements with data-pane chaptercode or data-cc-item), none has a panel level (0 elements with data-panel), none declares the page standard (no meta page-standard); at the first view the page does not scroll sideways at 390 px or at 1366 px (scrollWidth equals clientWidth in both), so the P1 overflow measure is not among the findings of this reading; the other page measures (P2 to P11) are taken by the page test the second task writes. TOOLS. The SEN0414 line has the template 9.50.0 (course_page_template_v9_50_0.html), the page builder v4_17_0, the page-data builder v2_24_0 and the page test 9.34.0 (with the exam-release checks, run by sen0414_page_test_run_v1_0_0.py against a TEST release key); it has no deck standard check, no deck overlap check and no chapter-code tab. The sibling course SEN0401 holds the finished versions of all of these (deck standard check v1_0_0, deck overlap check v1_0_0, page test 9.36.0, template 9.52.1, page builder v4_15_0, page-data builder v2_24_0), from the same ancestry as this line; they are ported as new-named copies, never edited. The chapter check v1_1_0 of this register reads the build checks of chapters 7 to 12 (chapter 6 has no entry in it). WRITTEN STANDARD (the owner's standing teaching-material rules; the sibling's measured standard, reused): DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. PLAN. Route: the deliverable (rebuilt decks and pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8, a chapter-code tab, a panel level, and the tools that measure the standard) is new content beside units that are Done (ST_Deck_Ch07, ST_Deck_Ch08, ST_Page_Ch07, ST_Page_Ch08 in this lineage; ST_Deck_Ch06 and ST_Page_Ch06 in the achieved first lineage): they stay Done and are not edited (G125, G133). The scope of this lineage excludes any change to the decks and pages of chapters 7 to 12 (ex:Excl2_NoRebuild), so new deliverables are a StageRevision from the Scope stage (G127), the route the sibling's register took for the same kind of request: this change request with its impact assessment first, then the retraction, four stage versions and a fill (seven versions), then the planning of the iteration and the brief per task. Order, as the owner's request and the tools demand: (1) the tooling port first - the deck standard check and deck overlap check (ST_Std_DeckTools), the page test 9.36.0, the page template 9.52.1 with its two builders and the regression control (ST_Std_PageTools); (2) then per chapter a deck story and a page story, chapter 6 first, then 7, then 8; the deck story of a chapter writes the chapter-code manifest the page story reads; chapters build in parallel where files do not collide (each chapter owns its own folders); a Verify task per deliverable is the controller's: it re-runs the checks, renders every slide, and records Done or NOT MET plainly. Stories (one acceptance criterion per unit, G133; each criterion names its tool and version, G136): ST_Std_DeckTools, ST_Std_PageTools, ST_Std_Deck_Ch06, ST_Std_Page_Ch06, ST_Std_Deck_Ch07, ST_Std_Page_Ch07, ST_Std_Deck_Ch08, ST_Std_Page_Ch08; 16 tasks, each naming its executor session. Iteration: a new iteration Iter_18 of constant length: 7 days (the class cadence: iteration end before the Friday class at 14:00 Istanbul), from the instant of the planning ceremony; the iterations of the first lineage were of changing length (end dates one to seven weeks out), so the length is the lineage agent's proposal to the owner, stated as a stipulation and kept constant from here on (G9). Estimated starts follow G120: hours after the executors begin (T0); nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun. Not in the plan: any chapter other than 6, 7 and 8; the held rework of chapters 1, 2 and 4 (ex:Excl2_ReworkHeld stays); the Mission outcome and the Achieved status (the owner's act); any change to a gate, a test, a template or a threshold other than the NEW files named in the tasks. What moves: the digests of the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog stages of the second lineage move once, when the stages are closed again; its status steps back to Opened and forward again through the revision; no Done story is re-dated or re-opened; the first lineage is not touched, and its Done chapter 6 stories stay as they are. Risks: the new template is a new file used only by pages built from it, so the shipped pages are compared with their stored results again only through the control set of TK_Std_Regress; a deck may not reach full concept coverage, in which case the coverage is stated as measured and not claimed; the machine has two cores, so browser tests run one at a time and the page tasks queue behind each other. A criterion that fails is named failing and its story is not Done; nothing is waived." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Scope1 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Scope stage: the chapter 6, 7 and 8 decks and pages are brought to the written standard"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_Standard, ex:IA2_Standard ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Owner's request of Friday 2026-10-23 08:57 Istanbul (05:57 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator in the assignment to the lineage agent and recorded here as relayed (a statement of its content, not a verbatim quotation, because the lineage agent holds the assignment, not a transcript of the owner's message): the PPT decks and interactive HTML pages of SEN0414 chapters 6 (Lists), 7 (Dictionaries) and 8 must meet the same standards as the sibling course SEN0401 chapters 5 and 6 just delivered, especially that the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in a special 'chapter code' tab of the page that can run it. The request is urgent: the owner's class material is needed as soon as possible, and decks and pages ship chapter by chapter as each is controlled. The request is direction from the owner and authorises the scope; the length of the iteration remains his to decide. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. The work adds deliverables (rebuilt decks and pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8, a page template, a page test and a deck check, all as new files); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage and its scope excludes any rebuild of the decks and pages of chapters 7 to 12, so a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The change request ex:CR2_Standard and the impact assessment ex:IA2_Standard were recorded first. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each, a sixth fills the last commit; the goals, objectives, stories and tasks already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The retracted outputs and their digests stay as history (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129). Recorded as decided by the lineage agent role: the route is what the owner's request needs; the stage revision itself he did not decide." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_Scope, ex:Out2_Goal, ex:Out2_Objective, ex:Out2_Backlog ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "f266274" .
ex:Out2_Scope backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out2_Goal backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out2_Objective backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out2_Backlog backlog:outputRetracted true .

