ex:AC2S_DeckCheck a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The deck standard check and the deck overlap check are new files that reproduce the measured facts of the three existing decks and measure D1 to D12"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard). Given the existing decks of chapters 6, 7 and 8, when the NEW files sen0414_deck_standard_check_v1_0_0.py and sen0414_deck_overlap_check_v1_0_0.py are written and run on them, then ALL of: (1) the files are new and no committed file is edited; (2) the deck check reports one named exit-coded result for each element D1 to D12 of the deck standard and prints the measured number; (3) on the existing decks it reproduces the measured facts of ex:IA2_Standard - chapter 6: 26 slides, 12 code slides, 3 native charts, 27 research concepts, failing D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11; chapter 7: 26 slides, 9 code slides, 1 native chart, 34 concepts, failing D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D11, D10 not measured; chapter 8: 25 slides, 13 code slides, 0 native charts, 57 concepts, the same failing set as chapter 7 - or explains every difference by reading the deck, settles the D8 discrepancy of the chapter 8 deck, and exits non-zero on all three; (4) the header defines each measure; (5) the check measures that a chapter-code manifest equals the deck's code boxes in text and order; (6) the logs of the runs are kept; results as printed; if any element fails the file is named failing. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS2_DeckOverlap ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2S_Tool_Passes, ex:TC2S_Tool_NotClaimed .

ex:AC2S_PageTest a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page test 9.36.0 is a new file that keeps every feature of 9.34.0 and fails the existing pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8 on the measured defects"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard). Given the page test 9.34.0 (SHA-256 recorded by the executor) and the existing pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8, when the NEW file sen0414_page_test_v9_36_0.py is written, then ALL of: (1) the file is new and 9.34.0 is byte-identical; (2) every feature text of 9.34.0 is present unchanged (a diff shows only added code and the version line and comments); (3) the added features P1, P2, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9, P11 apply to a page that declares the standard and are reported SKIP with the reason otherwise; FORCE_STANDARD=1 applies them to any page; (4) with FORCE_STANDARD=1 on the existing pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8 the run fails the features that name the measured defects (no chapter-code tab, no panel level, no declared standard) and ends without a crash; (5) the logs are kept; results as printed. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_PageTest36, ex:TS2_PageTest34 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2S_Tool_Passes, ex:TC2S_Tool_NotClaimed .

ex:AC2S_Template a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page template 9.52.1 and its two builders are new files that implement the panel level, the tab and tree rule, the chapter-code tab and the playground by name"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard). Given the page template 9.50.0, the page builder v4_17_0 and the page-data builder v2_24_0 (all byte-identical after the task), when the NEW files course_page_template_v9_52_1.html, sen0414_page_build_v4_18_0.py and sen0414_page_data_v2_25_0.py are made, then ALL of: (1) the files are new, the old ones byte-identical; (2) the template implements the DOM contract and keeps every id and hook of 9.50.0; the report states as a fact how the page runs code today and what runtime the chapter-library examples need; (3) a scratch page of chapter 1 and of chapter 10 built on 9.52.1 declares the page standard and the page test 9.36.0 passes P1, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9 on them (the chapter-code tab features apply when a manifest exists); (4) no gate, test or threshold is changed; results as printed. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_PageTemplate, ex:TS2_PageBuilder, ex:TS2_PageData, ex:TS2_PageTest36 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2S_Tool_Passes, ex:TC2S_Tool_NotClaimed .

ex:AC2S_Regress a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The new template gives the old page test the stored result on a control set of pages built from it"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard). Given the template 9.52.1, the builders v4_18_0 and v2_25_0 and the page tests, when the pages of chapters 1 and 10 are built into a scratch folder on the new template and the page test 9.34.0 is run on each, serially, then ALL of: (1) each run ends exit 0 with no failed feature and widgets, features and gates not below the stored result of the shipped page, skipped features not more and each of them one the stored result skips; (2) every run is kept as a log; (3) no committed file is edited, the scratch pages are not shipped; results as printed. Control set justified: the new template is a new file used only by pages built from it; the shipped pages stay on their files, so their results cannot move." ;
