ex:AC2S_Deck_Ch06 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The deck of chapter 6 meets every element of the deck standard, with its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard): the owner asks that the chapter 6 deck meet the same standards as the sibling course's chapters 5 and 6. Given the existing deck of chapter 6 and its research, when the deck is rebuilt as a new file with a new version number and its chapter-code manifest written, then ALL of: (1) the deck standard check v1_0_0 for chapter 6 reports every element D1 to D12 met and exits 0; (2) the deck overlap check v1_0_0 reports no overlap; (3) the chapter-code manifest chapter_code_ch06_v1_0_0.json lists the deck's code examples in slide order, by name, and its code and order equal the deck's code boxes (measured by the deck check); (4) the chapter's own build checks that exist for it pass (the chapter check v1_1_0 Deck/Ch06 where it covers the chapter); (5) no committed file is edited; results as printed; if any element fails the deck is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS2_DeckOverlap, ex:TS2_ChapterCheck ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
