ex:CR2_Charset a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Repair: the character-set declaration of the page template and of the pages lies beyond the first 1,024 bytes; repairs re-rank the open work"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope2 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's standing instruction of Friday 2026-10-23 11:07 Istanbul (08:07 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed (content, not a verbatim quotation): \"Repairs should change the priority of the PBIs or the tasks.\" When a repair or defect story enters the backlog, the open items are re-scored with the register's own ranking discipline (PriorityScore, inputs stated from observable facts), the new ranking is recorded as dated records, starts are ordered by it, and a repair outranks the work it blocks or that would ship the same defect. Known case to apply now: the SEN0401 sibling found that its page template placed the character-set declaration at byte ~13,600 (beyond the first 1,024 bytes), so pages show mojibake in prescan-only viewers; the SEN0414 template line and its pages 9.28.0 are to be checked for the same fault, a page task that would ship it is ranked behind the template task that places the declaration first in head, and the page test must check it. The scope does not move outward: the repair concerns files the scope already names (the new template 9.52.1 and the new page test 9.36.0, ex:Del2_StdTools); what is added is a requirement, a repair story with a controller task, a re-scoring of the open stories and a dependency of the page builds on the repair. Pending until the ScopeChange in the Backlog version." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_Charset a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the character-set repair changes in the iteration, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_Charset ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, read-only, 2026-10-23; byte offset of the first <meta charset=...> in the file): template 9.48.0 byte 13469, 9.49.0 byte 14037, 9.50.0 byte 15897 (the template line the new template 9.52.1 is ported over); the sibling's template 9.52.1 byte 13587 (head opens at byte 383), so porting the sibling's file would ship the fault; the shipped pages sen0414_ch06_page_v9_28_0.html, ch07 and ch08: byte 9293 each (head opens at byte 31). The page test 9.34.0 of this line has no check of the declaration (no occurrence of charset in the file). The HTML standard's encoding sniffing reads only the first 1,024 bytes for a declaration, so a declaration after that is not seen by a prescan-only viewer. The same holds for the shipped pages of the other chapters built from the same template; they are outside this iteration and are reported, not changed. CHARSET RULE (added to the page standard by this change): the page declares <meta charset=\"utf-8\"> as the FIRST child of <head>, so that its first byte lies below byte 1,024 of the file (the sibling's evidence needs the declaration within the first 1,024 bytes; the lineage's check requires it within the first 512). The template 9.52.1 places it first in head, before any comment, style or script; the builders keep it there; the page test 9.36.0 has a named feature P12 that reads the raw bytes of the built page (not the DOM) and fails when the declaration is absent or begins at or beyond byte 512; FORCE_STANDARD=1 and the declared standard both apply it, and it is never reported as SKIP for a page built from the new template. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage of the second lineage is revised once (the digest moves because a story and a task are added); no task has begun, so nothing is re-dated; the page builds of chapters 6, 7 and 8 gain a dependency on the repair's verification, which the controller records only when the template and the page test carry the rule; the open stories are re-scored with WSJF (inputs stated from observable facts) and the order of starts follows the score. The six tasks that can start now (the three tooling tasks and the three deck builds) are independent of the repair and start at once; the repair is carried inside the template and page-test tasks (the requirement is added to their briefs) and controlled by TK_Std_Charset_Verify. Not in the plan: the pages of other chapters built from the same template (reported, not changed); any edit of a committed file." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Backlog2 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Backlog stage: the character-set repair and the re-ranking of the open work"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_Charset, ex:IA2_Charset ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Owner's standing instruction of Friday 2026-10-23 11:07 Istanbul (08:07 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed (content, not a verbatim quotation): \"Repairs should change the priority of the PBIs or the tasks.\" When a repair or defect story enters the backlog, the open items are re-scored with the register's own ranking discipline (PriorityScore, inputs stated from observable facts), the new ranking is recorded as dated records, starts are ordered by it, and a repair outranks the work it blocks or that would ship the same defect. Known case to apply now: the SEN0401 sibling found that its page template placed the character-set declaration at byte ~13,600 (beyond the first 1,024 bytes), so pages show mojibake in prescan-only viewers; the SEN0414 template line and its pages 9.28.0 are to be checked for the same fault, a page task that would ship it is ranked behind the template task that places the declaration first in head, and the page test must check it. A story and a task are added to the lineage's closed Backlog stage, which moves its digest (G117, G125 route 2): this is a StageRevision from the Backlog stage, never from the Mission; the change request ex:CR2_Charset and the impact assessment ex:IA2_Charset were recorded first. This version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out2_BacklogR1 and rebuilds nothing; the next version closes the Backlog stage again as ex:Out2_BacklogR2 and re-admits every item, the stories and tasks of the iteration included, without re-dating them; a third version fills the commit. No task has begun, so nothing is lost by the retraction. The retracted output and its digest stay as history (L-112)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR1 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "9d46d05" .
ex:Out2_BacklogR1 backlog:outputRetracted true .

ex:Score2R_ST_Std_Charset a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ;
    backlog:hasScoreValue "48.00"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:scoredAt "2026-10-23T08:32:34"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:isAveragedFromMembers false ;
    backlog:hasScoreRationale "WSJF = (business value 8 + time criticality 20 + risk reduction 20) / job size 1.0 h = 48.00. Re-scored on Friday 2026-10-23 11:07 Istanbul (08:07 UTC) under the owner's standing instruction that repairs re-rank the open work. Inputs from observable facts: job size is the sum of the story's task estimates in this register; time criticality 20 = the class of 2026-10-23 or work that blocks it, 13 = blocks later work, 8 = later in the chapter order; the repair: a defect that every page built from the template ships (3 pages in this iteration, measured byte 15897 against a limit of 1024); it blocks 3 page stories (dependsOn) and is cheapest now, while the template and page-test tasks are being written. The previous state was 'not scored' (a direct owner order); this record replaces that flag and ranks the starts." .
