ex:TK_Std_Page_Ch07_Build backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_Charset_Verify .
ex:TK_Std_Page_Ch08_Build backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_Charset_Verify .
ex:TK_Std_Template backlog:hasAuditNote "REPAIR REQUIREMENT (ex:CR2_Charset, owner's standing instruction of 2026-10-23 11:07 Istanbul): the template 9.50.0 and the sibling's 9.52.1 place the character-set declaration at byte 15897 and 13587; the NEW template 9.52.1 must place <meta charset=\"utf-8\"> as the first child of <head>, before any comment, style or script, below byte 512, and the builders must keep it there. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, read-only, 2026-10-23; byte offset of the first <meta charset=...> in the file): template 9.48.0 byte 13469, 9.49.0 byte 14037, 9.50.0 byte 15897 (the template line the new template 9.52.1 is ported over); the sibling's template 9.52.1 byte 13587 (head opens at byte 383), so porting the sibling's file would ship the fault; the shipped pages sen0414_ch06_page_v9_28_0.html, ch07 and ch08: byte 9293 each (head opens at byte 31). The page test 9.34.0 of this line has no check of the declaration (no occurrence of charset in the file). The HTML standard's encoding sniffing reads only the first 1,024 bytes for a declaration, so a declaration after that is not seen by a prescan-only viewer. The same holds for the shipped pages of the other chapters built from the same template; they are outside this iteration and are reported, not changed." .
ex:TK_Std_PageTest backlog:hasAuditNote "REPAIR REQUIREMENT (ex:CR2_Charset, owner's standing instruction of 2026-10-23 11:07 Istanbul): add the named feature P12 to the NEW page test 9.36.0: it reads the raw bytes of the built page (not the DOM) and fails when no <meta charset> is present or its first byte lies at or beyond byte 512; it is applied to every page built from the new template, with the declared standard or FORCE_STANDARD=1, and is reported SKIP only for a page that does not declare the standard; prove it fails on the shipped pages (v9_28_0, byte 9293) and on a copy of the template 9.50.0 and passes on a page with the declaration first in head. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, read-only, 2026-10-23; byte offset of the first <meta charset=...> in the file): template 9.48.0 byte 13469, 9.49.0 byte 14037, 9.50.0 byte 15897 (the template line the new template 9.52.1 is ported over); the sibling's template 9.52.1 byte 13587 (head opens at byte 383), so porting the sibling's file would ship the fault; the shipped pages sen0414_ch06_page_v9_28_0.html, ch07 and ch08: byte 9293 each (head opens at byte 31). The page test 9.34.0 of this line has no check of the declaration (no occurrence of charset in the file). The HTML standard's encoding sniffing reads only the first 1,024 bytes for a declaration, so a declaration after that is not seen by a prescan-only viewer. The same holds for the shipped pages of the other chapters built from the same template; they are outside this iteration and are reported, not changed." .
