    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Owner's standing instruction of Friday 2026-10-23 11:07 Istanbul (08:07 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed (content, not a verbatim quotation): \"Repairs should change the priority of the PBIs or the tasks.\" When a repair or defect story enters the backlog, the open items are re-scored with the register's own ranking discipline (PriorityScore, inputs stated from observable facts), the new ranking is recorded as dated records, starts are ordered by it, and a repair outranks the work it blocks or that would ship the same defect. Known case to apply now: the SEN0401 sibling found that its page template placed the character-set declaration at byte ~13,600 (beyond the first 1,024 bytes), so pages show mojibake in prescan-only viewers; the SEN0414 template line and its pages 9.28.0 are to be checked for the same fault, a page task that would ship it is ranked behind the template task that places the declaration first in head, and the page test must check it. The boundary does not move outward in deliverables (ex:Del2_StdTools names the template and the page test); the repair story is admitted as the owner's standing rule requires." .
