ex:TK_Std_Regress backlog:hasAuditNote "Measured by the lineage agent on 2026-10-23, NOT MET (the task stays Proposed): on scratch pages of chapters 1 and 10 built on template 9.52.1 from the same page data, the page test 9.36.0 reports FAIL for two features of 9.34.0, 'a focused concept starts at the top' (first paragraph at 410 px on chapter 10 and 383 px on chapter 1, limit 240) and 'small phone (360px)'. The same chapter 10 page built on template 9.50.0 from the same data passes both (first paragraph at 210 px), and the shipped pages v9_28_0 pass both. The executor's own chapter 10 log shows PASS (first paragraph at 216 px, a different concept); the lineage agent re-ran the executor's own page file with its own driver and got FAIL. Logs: 08-tooling/control-iter18-logs/t36_01, t36_10, t36_old10, t36_ex10, t36_fx10 and t36_sh08. The repair of the template is a new story and task by the change route, ranked ahead of the page builds it would spoil." .
ex:TK_Std_PageTest backlog:hasAuditNote "FINDING by the lineage agent on 2026-10-23: the runner 08-tooling/sen0414_page_test_run_v1_0_0.py names the page test 9.34.0 in its code, so it never runs 9.36.0. A committed file is not edited: a new runner version naming 9.36.0 is a repair task, routed by the change route into the Backlog stage with a story, a criterion and a priority score; the control runs of the lineage agent use its own driver with a TEST release key." .

ex:CR2_Repair2 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Repair: the page template 9.52.1 shows its description as page text and the page-test runner never runs the new page test; repairs re-rank the open work"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope2 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's standing rule (2026-10-23, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed): \"Repairs should change the priority of the PBIs or the tasks.\" A repair entering the backlog re-ranks the open items with the register's own ranking discipline (PriorityScore, inputs from observable facts), the ranking is recorded as dated records, starts follow it, and a repair outranks the work it blocks. The course coordinator's direction of the same day: run the change route for both findings now, put the template repair (a new template version with its own check) and the runner repair ahead of the page builds, re-score dated, release the page builds only after the repairs are controlled; the owner is in class and needs the pages as soon as possible. The scope does not move outward: the repairs concern files the scope already names (the new template and the new page-test tools, ex:Del2_StdTools); what is added is two repair stories with controller tasks, a re-scoring of the open stories and dependencies of the page builds on the repairs. Pending until the ScopeChange that records it." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_Repair2 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the template and runner repairs change in the iteration, with the facts measured before they are planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_Repair2 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-23, Playwright 1.56.0, Chromium, 1400x900; repeatable). FINDING 1, the template: pages built on template 9.52.1 fail two features that 9.34.0 owns and that the shipped pages v9_28_0 and pages built on 9.50.0 from the same page data pass: 'a focused concept starts at the top' (first paragraph 410 px from the top, limit 240; 9.50.0: 210 px) and 'small phone (360px)' (the explorer-drawer check). ROOT CAUSE: the description comment at the head of course_page_template_v9_52_1.html (text carried over from the sibling's 9.52.0 and 9.52.1 descriptions) contains two literal '-->' sequences (36 comment closers against 34 openers); the first closes the comment at byte 1157, so about 1,157 characters of description prose are rendered as visible text of the page body above the header: the header starts at 190 px instead of 0, every concept sits 200 px lower, and at 360 px the layout of the drawer check changes. The comment of 9.50.0 is balanced (33 and 33). The character-set rule is not affected (the declaration stays at byte 37). The executor's own chapter 10 log shows both features passing; the lineage agent re-ran the executor's own scratch page file with its own driver and got FAIL on both, so the difference lies in what the executor's run measured, not in the file (the repair task must state why). FINDING 2, the runner: 08-tooling/sen0414_page_test_run_v1_0_0.py names sen0414_page_test_v9_34_0.py in its code (line 24); a run through it never executes the features P1 to P12 of 9.36.0. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage of the second lineage is revised once more (a story, criterion, test cases and tasks are added; the digest moves); the tasks already Done stay Done and are not re-dated; the page builds of chapters 6, 7 and 8 (Ready, not begun) gain dependencies on the template repair's verification, the runner repair's verification and the open regression check, so they are released only after the repairs are controlled; the open stories are re-scored with WSJF (inputs from observable facts) and the starts follow the score: the repairs first. Not in the plan: pages of other chapters built from the same template (reported, not changed); any edit of a committed file." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Backlog3 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Backlog stage: the template and runner repairs and the re-ranking of the open work"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_Repair2, ex:IA2_Repair2 ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Owner's standing rule (2026-10-23, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed): \"Repairs should change the priority of the PBIs or the tasks.\" A repair entering the backlog re-ranks the open items with the register's own ranking discipline (PriorityScore, inputs from observable facts), the ranking is recorded as dated records, starts follow it, and a repair outranks the work it blocks. The course coordinator's direction of the same day: run the change route for both findings now, put the template repair (a new template version with its own check) and the runner repair ahead of the page builds, re-score dated, release the page builds only after the repairs are controlled; the owner is in class and needs the pages as soon as possible. Stories, criteria and tasks are added to the lineage's closed Backlog stage, which moves its digest (G117, G125 route 2): a StageRevision from the Backlog stage, never from the Mission; the change request ex:CR2_Repair2 and the impact assessment ex:IA2_Repair2 were recorded first. This version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out2_BacklogR2 and rebuilds nothing; the next version closes the Backlog stage again as ex:Out2_BacklogR3 and re-admits every item, the Done tasks included, without re-dating them; a third version fills the commit. The retracted output and its digest stay as history (L-112)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR2 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "cb497a4be7b88feb26e25e8e85b032ba57a9c854" .
ex:Out2_BacklogR2 backlog:outputRetracted true .

ex:Score3R_ST_Std_TemplateFix a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ;
    backlog:hasScoreValue "32.00"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:scoredAt "2026-10-23T12:26:41"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:isAveragedFromMembers false ;
    backlog:hasScoreRationale "WSJF = (business value 8 + time criticality 20 + risk reduction 20) / job size 1.5 h = 32.00. Re-scored on 2026-10-23T12:26:41 UTC under the owner's rule that repairs re-rank the open work (ex:CR2_Repair2). Inputs from observable facts: job size is the sum of the story's task estimates in this register; time criticality 20 = the class of 2026-10-23 or work that blocks it, 13 = blocks later work, 8 = later in the chapter order; the repair of a template that shows its own description as page text; every page built from it would ship the defect and fail two old features; it blocks 3 page builds and is cheapest now, before any page is built. The earlier record is kept as history." .
