    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T12:43:39"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T16:25:56"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T19:48:08"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score7_ST_Std_Runner ; backlog:standsAlone true ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner's standing rule (2026-10-23, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed): \"Repairs should change the priority of the PBIs or the tasks.\" A repair entering the backlog re-ranks the open items with the register's own ranking discipline (PriorityScore, inputs from observable facts), the ranking is recorded as dated records, starts follow it, and a repair outranks the work it blocks. The course coordinator's direction of the same day: run the change route for both findings now, put the template repair (a new template version with its own check) and the runner repair ahead of the page builds, re-score dated, release the page builds only after the repairs are controlled; the owner is in class and needs the pages as soon as possible. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-23, Playwright 1.56.0, Chromium, 1400x900; repeatable). FINDING 1, the template: pages built on template 9.52.1 fail two features that 9.34.0 owns and that the shipped pages v9_28_0 and pages built on 9.50.0 from the same page data pass: 'a focused concept starts at the top' (first paragraph 410 px from the top, limit 240; 9.50.0: 210 px) and 'small phone (360px)' (the explorer-drawer check). ROOT CAUSE: the description comment at the head of course_page_template_v9_52_1.html (text carried over from the sibling's 9.52.0 and 9.52.1 descriptions) contains two literal '-->' sequences (36 comment closers against 34 openers); the first closes the comment at byte 1157, so about 1,157 characters of description prose are rendered as visible text of the page body above the header: the header starts at 190 px instead of 0, every concept sits 200 px lower, and at 360 px the layout of the drawer check changes. The comment of 9.50.0 is balanced (33 and 33). The character-set rule is not affected (the declaration stays at byte 37). The executor's own chapter 10 log shows both features passing; the lineage agent re-ran the executor's own scratch page file with its own driver and got FAIL on both, so the difference lies in what the executor's run measured, not in the file (the repair task must state why). FINDING 2, the runner: 08-tooling/sen0414_page_test_run_v1_0_0.py names sen0414_page_test_v9_34_0.py in its code (line 24); a run through it never executes the features P1 to P12 of 9.36.0." .

ex:TK_Std_Template_R2 a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Make page template 9.52.2 and builder 4.18.1: repair the early closing comment and guard against it"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Std_Template_R2" ; backlog:hasTitle "Make page template 9.52.2 and builder 4.18.1: repair the early closing comment and guard against it" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR4 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T12:43:39"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T16:25:56"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_templatefix, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_templatefix_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_templatefix_1 ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW files 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_2.html (from course_page_template_v9_52_1.html, which stays byte-identical) and 08-tooling/sen0414_page_build_v4_18_1.py (from sen0414_page_build_v4_18_0.py, byte-identical). ROOT CAUSE measured by the lineage agent (repeat it first and print it): the description comment at the head of 9.52.1 contains two literal '-->' sequences (36 closers against 34 openers; the first closes the comment at byte 1157), so about 1,157 characters of description prose are visible text above the header: header at 190 px instead of 0, first paragraph at 410 px instead of 210 on the same data. Repair: rewrite the comment so no '-->' lies inside it (keep the version history as text), keep everything else of 9.52.1 as it is (charset first in head below byte 512, ids, hooks, behaviour). The builder 4.18.1 differs from 4.18.0 only by the default template 9.52.2 and a guard: it refuses a template whose comment openers and closers differ in number or whose text between <body> and the header is not empty, and keeps the charset guard. Prove: (a) build scratch pages of chapters 1 and 10 on 9.52.2 (PAGE_SCRATCH and PAGE_DATA_DIR outside the repository; take the page data from the data builder 2.25.0 as before) and show the header at 0 px and no body text before it; (b) show that the guard refuses 9.52.1; (c) run the page tests 9.34.0 and 9.36.0 on both pages, one at a time, with the TEST key (your own key-substituting driver), and keep the logs: no [FAIL] line; (d) STATE WHY your earlier log of 9.52.1 on chapter 10 showed 'a focused concept starts at the top' and 'small phone' passing while the lineage agent's re-run of your page file failed: build the page again, compare it with the page you tested, and print the difference. Do not use the new runner or any file of the runner repair. Do not edit any committed file. Planned session SEN0414-I18-template-r2; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

