    backlog:hasAuditNote "OWNER DECISION of Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul (13:06 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed (content, not a verbatim quotation), a priority input: SEN0414 chapters 7, 8 and 9 are urgent for next week; chapter 6 drops behind them. After they are finished, return to ALL chapters starting with chapter 1 (retrofit to the standard: deck, chapter-code manifest, page), and after that build all remaining chapters. The coordinator's direction: add chapter 9 (deck, manifest, page) to Iter_18; check what exists for chapter 9; re-rank dated (chapters 7, 8, 9 deck and page ahead of the chapter 6 page, the repairs still first); plan the follow-on as planned work with estimates, not started now. The owner's standing rule that repairs re-rank the open items also holds. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-23, from the repository). CHAPTER 9 (Regular Expressions): research exists (03-materials/ch09/rdodi: document v1_0_0 and v1_0_1, domain TBox, ABox and SHACL, research v1_0_0); an old deck exists only as 08-tooling/ch09-deck/sen0414_ch09_deck_v1_0_0.pptx with its generator, examples and checks (03-materials/ch09 holds no deck); the old page exists as 03-materials/ch09/page/sen0414_ch09_page_v9_28_0.html (and 9_17_0, 9_18_0, 9_19_0): no chapter-code tab, no panel level, no declared standard, the character-set declaration at byte 9293; no chapter-code manifest exists. So chapter 9 needs a new deck (as a new file in 03-materials/ch09), its chapter-code manifest, then a new page, exactly as chapters 6, 7 and 8. OTHER CHAPTERS: chapters 1 to 5 and 10 to 24 have research, an old deck and an old page of the same kind (chapter 25, threads, has research, one deck file and one page file); none has a chapter-code manifest. ESTIMATES (the register's own, from the controlled chapters 6 to 8 of this iteration: a deck rebuild about 5.0 h of one executor session, a page rebuild about 4.0 h, the controller's control about 1.0 h per chapter): a retrofit of one chapter is about 10.0 h of work, about 9.0 h of it by executors; the 21 chapters 1 to 5 and 10 to 25 are about 210 h in all, about 70 h of wall time with three executor sessions in parallel (a deck session, a page session, a second chapter's deck session; the 2-core machine and the controller's control are the limit). Chapters still lacking research, deck or page after the retrofits are built from scratch at about 12.0 h each (research 3.0 h, deck 5.0 h, page 4.0 h); their list is measured when the retrofits finish. This story is the chapter 9 page." .

ex:TK_Std_Deck_Ch09_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Rebuild the deck of chapter 9 (Regular Expressions) against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Std_Deck_Ch09_Build" ; backlog:hasTitle "Rebuild the deck of chapter 9 (Regular Expressions) against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR4 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-24T19:37:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-24T19:58:33"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck09, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck09_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck09_1 ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Build the deck of chapter 9 as a NEW file with a new version number from the chapter research (03-materials/ch09/rdodi, the newest research) and the earlier deck's assets, to the deck standard; the new deck goes to 03-materials/ch09/ named as the chapter's earlier decks are named; the earlier chapter 9 deck lives in 08-tooling/ch09-deck/ and stays where it is. The owner's teaching-material rules: full sentences are fine but no long paragraphs (no text box over 30 words); explanation beside every code listing; the executed result shown as a visualization (native chart, table or drawn diagram) next to each listing; an everyday analogy for each key concept; 5N1K stories with real names, a real picture and a live link; native charts only; numbered slides; a resources slide; short speaker notes (at most 60 words); one smooth colour scheme; dividers that name their concepts with a line of meaning and a visual; coverage of the research concepts not below 90 percent. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch09/page/chapter_code_ch09_v1_0_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code exactly as on the slide, the slide number, the expected result), because the page tab must list the same examples in the same order. The deck generator is a NEW tool file in 08-tooling/ch09-deck; the checker is the independent TK_Std_DeckCheck (not yours): run it when it exists and report every element as printed. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I18-deck-ch09; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 5.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

ex:TK_Std_Deck_Ch09_Verify a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Verify the deck of chapter 9 against the deck standard"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Std_Deck_Ch09_Verify" ; backlog:hasTitle "Verify the deck of chapter 9 against the deck standard" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR4 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_Compliance ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Verify ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-24T19:55:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-24T19:58:33"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck09, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck09_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck09_1 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_Deck_Ch09_Build, ex:TK_Std_DeckCheck ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Run the deck standard check v1_0_0 and the deck overlap check v1_0_0 for chapter 9, the chapter's own build checks (the chapter check v1_1_0 where it covers the chapter), and read the deck slide by slide, rendering every slide to an image for visual review (the reading by the three roles of the owner's preference - teaching academician, reviewing faculty specialist, student - is recorded as a reading, not as a tool result); record every result as printed: Done or NOT MET, no waiver. Planned session SEN0414-lineage (control); estimated start T0+5h after the executors begin, about 0.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

ex:TK_Std_Page_Ch09_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Rebuild the page of chapter 9 (Regular Expressions) on the new template with the chapter-code tab"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Std_Page_Ch09_Build" ; backlog:hasTitle "Rebuild the page of chapter 9 (Regular Expressions) on the new template with the chapter-code tab" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR4 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:InProgress ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-24T20:05:26"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_Template, ex:TK_Std_PageTest, ex:TK_Std_Deck_Ch09_Verify ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Build the page of chapter 9 as a NEW file with a new page version (above 9_28_0) on the template 9.52.1 with the page builder v4_18_0 and the page-data builder v2_25_0 (state how you passed the template), from the chapter research, the deck's lecture export and stories, and the deck's chapter-code manifest. Run the page tests 9.36.0 and 9.34.0 (the runner sen0414_page_test_run_v1_0_0.py), serially, store the result as a new test_results file in 08-tooling/ch09-page, and run the chapter check Page/Ch09. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I18-page-ch09; estimated start T0+8.5h after the executors begin, about 3.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

ex:TK_Std_Page_Ch09_Verify a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Verify the page of chapter 9 against the page standard"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Std_Page_Ch09_Verify" ; backlog:hasTitle "Verify the page of chapter 9 against the page standard" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR4 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_Compliance ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Verify ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_Page_Ch09_Build ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Re-run serially the page tests 9.36.0 and 9.34.0, the chapter checks Research, Deck and Page for chapter 9 where they cover it, the deck match check and the manifest equality (the chapter-code tab equals the deck's code, text and order); open the page at 390, 768 and 1366 px and look at every tab; record every result as printed: Done or NOT MET, no waiver. Planned session SEN0414-lineage (control); estimated start T0+11.5h after the executors begin, about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

ex:AC2S_Deck_Ch09 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The deck of chapter 9 meets every element of the deck standard, with its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard): the owner asks that the chapter 9 deck meet the same standards as the sibling course's chapters 5 and 6. Given the existing deck of chapter 9 and its research, when the deck is rebuilt as a new file with a new version number and its chapter-code manifest written, then ALL of: (1) the deck standard check v1_0_0 for chapter 9 reports every element D1 to D12 met and exits 0; (2) the deck overlap check v1_0_0 reports no overlap; (3) the chapter-code manifest chapter_code_ch09_v1_0_0.json lists the deck's code examples in slide order, by name, and its code and order equal the deck's code boxes (measured by the deck check); (4) the chapter's own build checks that exist for it pass (the chapter check v1_1_0 Deck/Ch09 where it covers the chapter); (5) no committed file is edited; results as printed; if any element fails the deck is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS2_DeckOverlap, ex:TS2_ChapterCheck ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2S_D_Passes, ex:TC2S_D_NotClaimed .

ex:AC2S_Page_Ch09 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page of chapter 9 meets the page standard with the chapter-code tab in the deck's order"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard): the owner asks that the chapter 9 page meet the same standards as the sibling course's chapters 5 and 6, above all that the slide code appears in the same order in a chapter-code tab that runs it. Given the existing page of chapter 9 and the rebuilt deck of chapter 9, when the page is rebuilt as a new file with a new page version on the template 9.52.1 with the builders v4_18_0 and v2_25_0, then ALL of: (1) the page test 9.36.0 runs all its added features with no skip and passes them (P1, P2, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9, P11), exit 0; (2) the page test 9.34.0 reports no failure and widgets, features and gates not below the stored result of the existing page, skipped not more; (3) the chapter-code tab equals the deck's chapter-code manifest in names, code and order and each example runs in the page and shows its result (measured by the page test); (4) the chapter checks that exist for the chapter (Research, Page) pass; (5) no committed file is edited, no gate, test or threshold changed beyond the new files; the stored page-test result is a new file; results as printed; if any element fails the page is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS2_DeckOverlap, ex:TS2_PageTest36, ex:TS2_PageTemplate, ex:TS2_PageBuilder, ex:TS2_PageData, ex:TS2_PageTest34, ex:TS2_ChapterCheck, ex:TS2_RdodiGates ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2S_P_Passes, ex:TC2S_P_NotClaimed .
