ex:CR2_Retest37 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Page test 9.36.0 reads a chapter-code result before it has finished and flags an expected error message: a corrected SEN0414 page test 9.37.0 for the chapter 6 and chapter 9 page criteria"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope2 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-24, recorded as relayed: the known race in page test 9.36.0 (the chapter-code step reads an example's result while it still shows 'Running...') may hit the SEN0414 pages; the sibling course restated its page criteria on a corrected test 9.37.0; decide by the change route, without waiting for the owner, whether the chapter 6 and chapter 9 page criteria should name a corrected SEN0414 test, only if the executors actually hit it; disclose in one line. The owner's standing rule that work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with also holds. The scope does not move outward: the page tests are files the scope already names (ex:Del2_StdTools); what is added is one repair story with a build task and a controller task, and the restatement of two page criteria on the corrected test." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Pending .

ex:IA2_Retest37 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the corrected page test changes in the iteration, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_Retest37 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-24, Playwright 1.56.0, Chromium 1366x768): the executor of the chapter 6 page ran the page test 9.36.0 on its page (commit ff8dedf, log 08-tooling/ch06-page/logs_iter18/page_test_9_36_0_run1.log): exit with the feature 'P2 every chapter-code example opens in the editor, runs in the page ... and shows a visualised result' FAILING with 2 defects out of 24 examples: '2 Lists of lists and a wrong index' and '24 Coin Flip Streaks: result is text, not a visualisation'. The lineage agent's own probe of the same page (first example of a session: the page loads Python on the first run, 3.7 s) shows the cause of both: the test waits only until the result element holds ANY text (line 1597 of sen0414_page_test_v9_36_0.py: textContent length above 0 or an svg/canvas/img/table) and then reads after 300 ms; the page writes the placeholder 'Running...' into that element when Run is clicked, so a result slower than about 0.5 s is read as the text 'Running...' with no visual (examples 2 and 24 read exactly that: {t: 'Running...', v: false}); once the placeholder is gone the same examples show 'code -> Python -> lines in a result card (3716 ms and 622 ms) same result as on the slide' with the visual present. The second cause is separate: the test flags a result whose first 160 characters contain 'Error:' (line 1600), and chapter 6 example 2 is the book's IndexError demonstration, whose recorded expected result in the deck's manifest ends 'IndexError: list index out of range' and which the page reproduces ('same result as on the slide'); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 passed because their error demonstrations print the error name without a colon. The sibling's corrected file (/home/claude/sen0401/08-tooling/sen0401_page_test_v9_37_0.py, controlled in its register) changes only the wait for the placeholder; it does not touch the second cause. Pages that passed 9.36.0 (chapters 7 and 8) are unchanged and stay valid. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage of the second lineage is revised once more (a story, a criterion, test cases and two tasks are added; the criteria of the pages of chapters 6 and 9 name the page test 9.37.0 instead of 9.36.0; the digest moves); the tasks already Done stay Done and are not re-dated; the pages of chapters 7 and 8 are not affected (Done on 9.36.0, with no placeholder read and no error example); the verify tasks of the chapter 6 and chapter 9 pages gain the dependency on the controller task of the corrected test; the build tasks of those pages are not blocked (their executors run on); the open stories are re-scored. Not in the plan: any edit of a committed file or of the page test 9.36.0." .
